#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:21
msgid "The Narrative Principle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:23
#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:47
#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:374
msgid "From Neel Nanda"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:25
msgid ""
"\"A paper is a short, rigorous, evidence-based technical story with a "
"takeaway readers care about.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:27
msgid ""
"The narrative rests on three pillars that must be crystal clear by the "
"end of your introduction:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:29
msgid ""
"**The \"What\"**: One to three specific novel claims fitting within a "
"cohesive theme. Vague contributions like \"we study X\" fail "
"immediately—reviewers need precise, falsifiable claims."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:31
msgid ""
"**The \"Why\"**: Rigorous empirical evidence that convincingly supports "
"those claims, including strong baselines honestly tuned and experiments "
"that distinguish between competing hypotheses rather than merely showing "
"\"decent results.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:33
msgid ""
"**The \"So What\"**: Why readers should care, connecting your "
"contribution to problems the community recognizes as important."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:35
msgid "From Andrej Karpathy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:37
msgid ""
"\"A paper is not a random collection of experiments you report on. The "
"paper sells a single thing that was not obvious or present before. The "
"entire paper is organized around this core contribution with surgical "
"precision.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:39
msgid ""
"This applies whether you're presenting a new architecture, a theoretical "
"result, or improved understanding of existing methods—NeurIPS explicitly "
"notes that \"originality does not necessarily require an entirely new "
"method.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:41
msgid ""
"**Practical Implication**: If you cannot state your contribution in one "
"sentence, you don't yet have a paper. Everything else—experiments, "
"related work, discussion—exists only to support that core claim."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:45
msgid "Time Allocation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:49
msgid "Spend approximately **the same amount of time** on each of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:50
msgid "The abstract"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:51
msgid "The introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:52
msgid "The figures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:53
msgid "Everything else combined"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:55
msgid ""
"This isn't hyperbole—most reviewers form preliminary judgments before "
"reaching your methods section. Readers encounter your paper in a "
"predictable pattern: **title → abstract → introduction → figures → maybe "
"the rest.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:57
msgid "Reviewer Reading Patterns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:59
msgid "Studies of reviewer behavior show:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:60
#, python-format
msgid "Abstract is read 100% of the time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:61
msgid "Introduction is skimmed by 90%+ of reviewers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:62
msgid "Figures are examined before methods by most reviewers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:63
msgid "Full methods are read only if interest is established"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:65
msgid ""
"**Implication**: Front-load your paper's value. Don't bury the "
"contribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_writing-guide.md:69
msgid "Abstract Writing Formula"
msgstr ""

